X:1
T:Craigielee March
% NFF Book 2023
C:Thomas Edward Bulch (1862-1930)
S:collected from Thomas Edward Bulch
S:see also Waltzing Matilda
H:The Craigielee forms part of the "Waltzing Matilda" story. The tune is
H:based James Barr's composition (1818) "Thou Bonnie Woods of Craigielee".
H:It is not known how or when Thomas Bulch obtained a copy of James Barr's
H:composition but Bulch's orchestration for brass band was played at the
H:Warrnambool Races in April 1894 by the Warrnambool Garrison Artillery
H:Band. Christina Macpherson heard the tune and later played a version
H:of it for Banjo Paterson at Winton, in August 1895.
R:March
N:Arranged by Dave De Santi, Feb 1996
